  "live_records": {
    "q-39815": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39815",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
